 "$comment": "Which CMU trials become clips, and what each one is. Every one of the 55 paired two-person trials is here: subjects 18/19, 20/21, 22/23 and 33/34 are A/B recordings of the same takes, frame-synchronised in one world frame, so each entry names 'pair' and bakes both actors into a single cf.clip.v2 document, and the contact is the captured contact. An entry naming 'subject' instead bakes one performer alone: a solo action has no second body to synchronise with, and the two-person set holds no sustained run, so the running clips come from CMU's single-subject sprint trials. The tags are a controlled vocabulary, not free text, because retrieval depends on them - a query for comfort must not return a quarrel. 'affection' is the field that keeps the aggression half of this dataset out of an affectionate scene. Descriptions are CMU's own words, taken from the fetched trial index, with the '(2 subjects - subject A)' suffix removed.",
